-- Course: Bachelor of Dental Surgery (002788J)
UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<p>The Bachelor of Dental Surgery emphasises a holistic and preventive-based approach to oral health care. Integrate knowledge and understanding of relevant biological and medical sciences in managing patients. </p><p>You’ll also develop high levels of professionalism, including the ability to effectively monitor your performance. </p><p>Throughout your studies you’ll get the chance to explore a dynamic curriculum which uses an integrated learning approach. You''ll learn relevant scientific information as you develop your professional and clinical skills. </p><p> From first year, you’ll undertake compulsory clinical placements in a range of clinic settings. These may include hospital-based, community, rural and interstate locations. </p>',
    course_duration_per_week = 260,
    total_course_duration = '5 year(s) full-time only (no part time option)',
    offshore_tuition_fee = 104100,
    onshore_tuition_fee = NULL,
    entry_requirements = '<table><tbody><tr><td><strong>Academic Requirements</strong></td><td><ul><li>Admission is competitive; applicants must meet at least one minimum entry requirement, demonstrate prerequisites, sit UCAT ANZ, and attend interview if invited.</li><li>Secondary education (Year 12): Completion of qualification equivalent to SACE with adjusted ATAR equivalent selection rank of 90.00 or higher.</li><li>Higher education study: Successful completion of at least 6 months full-time (or equivalent part-time) in undergraduate diploma (AQF level 5) or higher at recognised institution with GPA 5.0 or higher.</li><li>International admissions by country with specified qualification and score: Australia ATAR 90; Bangladesh HSC 4.97; Canada OSSD 85%; China Gaokao 80%; Denmark Studentereksamen 7 (Good); France French Baccalaureate 13.5; Global IB 33; Hong Kong HKDSE 21; India CBSE and CISCE 85; India State Board 98; Indonesia SMA III 90%; Kenya KCSE A-; Malaysia Matrikulasi 3.33; Malaysia STPM 3.33; Malaysia UEC 11; Nepal NEB 3.61; Norway Upper Secondary School Certificate 4.8; Philippines High School Diploma K12 94%; Singapore GCE A Levels 12; South Korea CSAT 355; Sri Lanka GCE A Levels 12; Sweden Upper Secondary School Leaving Certificate 16.0; Taiwan GSAT 80%; Thailand Matayom 6 3.90; UK/Global GCE A Levels 12; USA/Global AP 12; USA/Global ACT 29; USA/Global SAT 1280; Vietnam Year 12 8.7.</li></ul></td></tr><tr><td><strong>English Proficiency</strong></td><td><ul><li>International students who speak English as additional language must have obtained one of following standards within last two years prior to admission.</li><li>IELTS Overall 7, Reading 7, Listening 7, Speaking 7, Writing 7.</li><li>Where previous study/work experience conducted in English, application must be accompanied by certified documentation certifying language of instruction/employment was English.</li><li>Equivalent English qualifications link provided by Adelaide University.</li></ul></td></tr><tr><td><strong>Interview</strong></td><td><ul><li>Applicants must attend an interview if invited.</li><li>If meet academic minimum entry requirements, selected for interview on basis of UCAT ANZ results.</li><li>Eligible applicants ranked on combination of UCAT ANZ, interview results and academic score.</li></ul></td></tr><tr><td><strong>Other</strong></td><td><ul><li>Applicants must sit University Clinical Aptitude Test (UCAT ANZ).</li><li>Recognition of prior learning: Credit may be granted for formal, informal, non-formal learning; use online Credit Assessor.</li><li>Possession of qualifications in addition to academic entry does not guarantee place; applications considered individually, selection competitive.</li></ul></td></tr></tbody></table>',
    apply_form = 'https://adelaideuni.edu.au/study/degrees/bachelor-of-dental-surgery/',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE cricos_course_code = '002788J';

-- Course: Master of Psychology (Health) (061743M)
UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<p>Adelaide University’s Master of Psychology (Health) is your path to becoming a registered psychologist. As one of only two health psychology degrees offered in Australia, it delivers comprehensive training in both health promotion and clinical health psychology. </p><p>With a focus on promoting healthier lifestyles and clinical health care, you’ll acquire a diverse set of skills relevant to a variety of careers as a psychologist. Learn to assess a broad range of clients and develop treatments to address issues like anxiety, depression and pain. Understand chronic illness management and how to support patients dealing with trauma, disability and rehabilitation. Gain an evidence-based approach to clinical practice and an understanding of how psychology can be used to advance public health. </p><p>Across 1000 hours and three industry placements, you’ll develop the skills to master behavioural change techniques to help people sustain healthier habits and conduct psychological assessments to create personalised intervention strategies.</p>',
    course_duration_per_week = 104,
    total_course_duration = '2 year(s) full-time',
    offshore_tuition_fee = 52200,
    onshore_tuition_fee = NULL,
    entry_requirements = '<table><tbody><tr><td><strong>Academic Requirements</strong></td><td>A completed four-year psychology honours degree with at least an upper second class or equivalent overall mark, or an equivalent degree that is accredited by the Australian Psychology Accreditation Council</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Other</strong></td><td><ul><li>Undertake the Casper Situational Judgement Test (CSJT)</li><li>Provide two referee reports via the HODSPA – VTAC reference portal system</li><li>In cases where there are more eligible applicants than available places, admission will be competitive with ranks based on the entry criteria</li><li>Recognition of prior learning: Adelaide University is committed to recognising the contribution of students’ prior learning towards their program requirements. Credit may be granted for formal, informal, and non-formal learning. Visit the Credit for previous study page for more information. Answer a few simple questions with our online Credit Assessor to see what credit you could get.</li></ul></td></tr><tr><td><strong>Interview</strong></td><td>Attend an interview, if invited</td></tr><tr><td><strong>English Proficiency</strong></td><td><ul><li>International students who speak English as an additional language must have obtained one of the following standards within the last two years prior to admission</li><li>Where previous study/work experience was conducted in English, the application must be accompanied by certified documentation from the educational institution/employer certifying that the language of instruction/employment was English</li><li>IELTS Overall 7</li><li>IELTS Reading 7</li><li>IELTS Listening 7</li><li>IELTS Speaking 7</li><li>IELTS Writing 7</li><li>Please access the following link for a comprehensive list of English language tests accepted by Adelaide University and other important information in relation to meeting the University’s language requirements: Equivalent English qualifications</li></ul></td></tr></tbody></table>',
    apply_form = 'https://adelaideuni.edu.au/study/degrees/master-of-psychology-health/',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE cricos_course_code = '061743M';

-- Course: Bachelor of Veterinary Technology (0100494)
UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<p>Our Bachelor of Veterinary Technology is a clinically focused degree and provides access to our world-class, $37 million veterinary health centre. You''ll build high-level expertise in the nursing care of animals of all kinds – from cats, dogs and horses to farm animals, wildlife and exotic pets.</p><p>Gain hands-on animal and clinical experience through work placements providing you with opportunities to learn and experience the diversity of veterinary nursing and technology practice. Build an invaluable community of peers as you collaborate with animal and veterinary scientists, animal behaviourists and veterinarians.</p><p>Study the complete spectrum of animal health, including pathology, pain management, animal nutrition, dentistry and pharmacology. Gain knowledge and training in the use of veterinary anaesthetic, radiography and dental equipment. Explore animal diseases, including those threatening humans, and the concept of One Health.</p><p>You’ll graduate with extensive real-world experience, ready for fulfilling careers in general veterinary practice and specialist hospitals, animal breeding farms, zoos and animal shelters.</p>',
    course_duration_per_week = 156,
    total_course_duration = '3 year(s) full-time',
    offshore_tuition_fee = 56600,
    onshore_tuition_fee = NULL,
