ed Placement (AP) 7</li><li>USA / Global America College Test (ACT) 21</li><li>USA / Global Scholastic Assessment Test (SAT) 1100</li><li>Vietnam Bằng Tốt Nghiệp Trung Học Phổ Thông (Vietnamese Year 12) 7.8</li></ul></td></tr><tr><td><strong>English Proficiency</strong></td><td><ul><li>International students who speak English as an additional language must have obtained one of the following standards within the last two years prior to admission</li><li>Where previous study/work experience was conducted in English, the application must be accompanied by certified documentation from the educational institution/employer certifying that the language of instruction/employment was English</li><li>IELTS Overall 6.5</li><li>IELTS Reading 6</li><li>IELTS Listening 6</li><li>IELTS Speaking 6</li><li>IELTS Writing 6</li><li>Equivalent English qualifications link available for comprehensive list of English language tests accepted</li></ul></td></tr><tr><td><strong>Interview</strong></td><td><ul><li>All applicants are required to register for an audition which involves dance, acting and singing components, as well as an interview</li><li>Selection will be based on audition score as long as academic thresholds are met</li><li>Auditions take place in November each year in Adelaide, Melbourne, Brisbane and Perth</li><li>Auditionees are strongly encouraged to attend a live audition, but domestic and international applicants who cannot attend an in-person audition, may request to submit a recorded audition when completing your registration form</li><li>Complete the Bachelor of Music Theatre registration audition form</li><li>Pay the non-refundable audition registration fee online via our online portal</li><li>Read the audition requirements and prepare your material</li><li>Contact auditions@adelaide.edu.au for fee or payment questions</li></ul></td></tr><tr><td><strong>Other</strong></td><td><ul><li>Adelaide University is committed to recognising the contribution of students’ prior learning towards their program requirements</li><li>Credit may be granted for formal, informal, and non-formal learning</li><li>Online Credit Assessor available to see what credit you could get</li><li>Possession of English qualifications, in addition to academic entry requirements, does not guarantee a place; applications considered individually and selection is competitive</li></ul></td></tr></tbody></table>',
