-- Course: Doctor of Veterinary Medicine (086311G)
UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<p>Our Doctor of Veterinary Medicine provides the necessary training and qualifications for registration as a veterinarian.</p><p>Learn about the causes, diagnosis, treatment and prevention of diseases in domesticated animals, including dogs, cats, horses, ruminants, camelids, pigs, poultry and wildlife.</p><p>Hone your scientific and technical skills for research and clinical practice. Gain advanced professional experience through a structured workplace-based program. Complete 26 weeks of extramural practical work.</p><p>Practise communicating with pet owners, farm managers and other stakeholders about animal care, treatment and preventative health measures. Protect public health and animal product quality. Develop your professional conduct, including teamwork, resilience, self-awareness and leadership skills.</p><p>You’ll graduate ready to register as a veterinarian in Australasia – equipped for roles that could include clinical practice, zoos, aquariums, research, consultancy, public health, wildlife conservation and animal welfare.</p>',
    course_duration_per_week = 156,
    total_course_duration = '3 year(s) full-time only (no part time option)',
    offshore_tuition_fee = 81400,
    onshore_tuition_fee = NULL,
    entry_requirements = '<table><tbody><tr><td><strong>Academic Requirements</strong></td><td><ul><li>A completed Bachelor of Science (Veterinary Bioscience) from the University of Adelaide or Adelaide University</li><li>Doctor of Veterinary Medicine does not accept direct applications</li></ul></td></tr><tr><td><strong>Recognition of Prior Learning</strong></td><td><ul><li>Credit may be granted for formal, informal, and non-formal learning</li><li>Use online Credit Assessor to see what credit you could get</li></ul></td></tr><tr><td><strong>English Proficiency</strong></td><td><ul><li>International students who speak English as an additional language must have obtained one of the following standards within the last two years prior to admission</li><li>IELTS Overall 7</li><li>IELTS Reading 7</li><li>IELTS Listening 7</li><li>IELTS Speaking 7</li><li>IELTS Writing 7</li><li>Where previous study/work experience was conducted in English, application must be accompanied by certified documentation certifying language of instruction/employment was English</li><li>Possession of qualifications in addition to academic entry requirements does not guarantee a place; applications considered individually and selection is competitive</li></ul></td></tr></tbody></table>',
    apply_form = 'https://adelaideuni.edu.au/study/degrees/doctor-of-veterinary-medicine/',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE cricos_course_code = '086311G';

-- Course: Master of Architecture (059319A)
UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<p>Our Master of Architecture equips you with advanced expertise in architectural design, its relationship with the environment, culture, and advancements in design and construction technologies. </p><p>Develop the technical and creative skills across advanced contemporary architecture courses that foster collaborative and innovative research practices. </p><p>You''ll learn in purpose-designed facilities including dedicated design studios and workshops. Here, you’ll engage with industry professionals and real clients to develop solutions that respond to real-world challenges. </p><p>Our students can expect to explore career paths in a range of industries once they graduate. This degree can also lead to higher degrees by research or complementing further study.</p>',
    course_duration_per_week = 104,
    total_course_duration = '2 year(s) full-time',
    offshore_tuition_fee = 50500,
    onshore_tuition_fee = NULL,
    entry_requirements = '<table><tbody><tr><td><strong>Academic Requirements</strong></td><td><ul><li>A completed Bachelor of Architectural Design; OR a 3-year pre-professional architecture program from a recognised Australian higher education institution or equivalent</li><li>GPA equivalent to an Adelaide University 4.0 on a 7-point scale for entry</li><li>Applicants with a bachelor degree in architecture from a non-Australian institution may be considered and will be required to provide a portfolio</li><li>Portfolio should include own creative works from previous degrees, professional, and/or personal background, showing design skills, knowledge, and familiarity with a range of design tools and media</li><li>Portfolio should comprise evidence of design process, development and drawing documentation in addition to final outcomes</li><li>Portfolio may include material developed with others if clearly referenced and the applicant''s contribution explained</li></ul></td></tr><tr><td><strong>English Proficiency</strong></td><td><ul><li>International students who speak English as an additional language must have obtained one of the following standards within the last two years prior to admission</li><li>Where previous study/work experience was conducted in English, the application must be accompanied by certified documentation from the educational institution/employer certifying that the language of instruction/employment was English</li><li>IELTS Overall 6.5</li><li>IELTS Reading 6</li><li>IELTS Listening 6</li><li>IELTS Speaking 6</li><li>IELTS Writing 6</li></ul></td></tr><tr><td><strong>Other</strong></td><td><ul><li>In cases where there are more eligible applicants than available places, admission will be competitive with ranks based on the entry criteria</li><li>Possession of qualifications, in addition to the academic entry requirements, does not in itself guarantee a place; applications considered individually and selection is competitive</li><li>Adelaide University recognises prior learning; credit may be granted for formal, informal, and non-formal learning</li></ul></td></tr></tbody></table>',
    apply_form = 'https://adelaideuni.edu.au/study/degrees/master-of-architecture/',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE cricos_course_code = '059319A';

-- Course: Bachelor of Architectural Design (002782D)
UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<p>Make an impact with your creative problem-solving abilities in the broad ranging field of architecture, where you could do anything from helping to preserve treasured heritage sites to designing inclusive and sustainable architecture of the future.</p><p>The Bachelor of Architectural Design will equip you with the problem-solving skills and creative expertise needed to tackle design challenges through an ethical understanding of culture and the natural environment.</p><p>You’ll learn how to design projects of varying scales and complexities, overcoming obstacles to deliver sustainable solutions. You’ll become an effective communicator, understanding how to co-design projects that realise your client’s vision.</p>',
    course_duration_per_week = 156,
    total_course_duration = '3 year(s) full-time',
    offshore_tuition_fee = 50500,
    onshore_tuition_fee = NULL,
