-- Course: Bachelor of Oral Health (036335B)
UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<p>Our Bachelor of Oral Health is a three-year, evidence-based degree that sets you up for a rewarding career in oral health. </p><p>You’ll learn about the anatomy and physiology of teeth, gums and oral tissues – and how they impact overall health. Discover how to identify and treat common dental conditions, while developing the communication and people skills needed to make a difference in your community. </p><p>You’ll train in high-tech facilities, including our dental simulation clinic. Extensive clinical placements will provide real-world experience working with clients. Under expert guidance and supervision, you’ll build the confidence and skills to excel in a people-centred career. You’ll also have the chance to give back to society – providing essential dental care to those in need via our dental outreach program. </p><p>By graduation, you’ll have the clinical and professional skills to launch your career in oral health therapy, hygiene and promotion. </p>',
    course_duration_per_week = 156,
    total_course_duration = '3 year(s) full-time only (no part time option)',
    offshore_tuition_fee = 69800,
    onshore_tuition_fee = NULL,
    entry_requirements = '<table><tbody><tr><td><strong>Academic Requirements</strong></td><td><ul><li>Admission is competitive; applicants must meet at least one minimum entry requirement, demonstrate prerequisites, sit UCAT ANZ, and attend interview if invited.</li><li>Secondary education (Year 12): Completion of qualification equivalent to SACE with adjusted ATAR equivalent selection rank of 70.00 or higher.</li><li>VET: Completion of an award from an RTO at Diploma (AQF level 5) or higher.</li><li>Higher education study: Successful completion of at least 6 months full-time study (or equivalent part-time) in undergraduate diploma (AQF level 5) or higher at recognised HE institution with GPA 4.0 or higher.</li><li>International admissions by country with specified qualification and score: Australia ATAR 70; Bangladesh HSC 4.80; Canada OSSD 65%; China Gaokao 60%; Denmark Studentereksamen 4 (Fair); France French Baccalaureate 11.0; Global IB 25; Hong Kong HKDSE 16; India CBSE and CISCE 65; India State Board 80; Indonesia SMA III 75%; Kenya KCSE B+; Malaysia Matrikulasi 2.67; Malaysia STPM 2.67; Malaysia UEC 23; Nepal NEB 2.81; Norway Upper Secondary School Certificate 3.2; Philippines High School Diploma (Grade 12 Academic Track) K12 86%; Singapore GCE A Levels 7; South Korea CSAT 300; Sri Lanka GCE A Levels 8; Sweden Upper Secondary School Leaving Certificate 13.0; Taiwan GSAT 60%; Thailand Matayom 6 3.20; UK/Global GCE A Levels 7; USA/Global AP 7; USA/Global ACT 21; USA/Global SAT 1100; Vietnam Year 12 7.8.</li></ul></td></tr><tr><td><strong>English Proficiency</strong></td><td><ul><li>International students who speak English as additional language must have obtained one of the following within last two years prior to admission.</li><li>IELTS: Overall 7, Reading 7, Listening 7, Speaking 7, Writing 7.</li><li>Where previous study/work experience was conducted in English, application must be accompanied by certified documentation certifying language of instruction/employment was English.</li><li>Equivalent English qualifications: see Adelaide University link for comprehensive list.</li></ul></td></tr><tr><td><strong>Interview</strong></td><td><ul><li>Attend an interview if invited.</li><li>If applicants meet academic minimum entry requirements, selected for interview on basis of UCAT ANZ results.</li><li>Eligible applicants ranked on combination of UCAT ANZ, interview results and academic score.</li></ul></td></tr><tr><td><strong>Other</strong></td><td><ul><li>Sit the University Clinical Aptitude Test (UCAT ANZ).</li><li>Recognition of prior learning: Credit may be granted for formal, informal, non-formal learning; use online Credit Assessor.</li><li>Possession of qualifications in addition to academic entry does not guarantee place; applications considered individually, selection competitive.</li></ul></td></tr></tbody></table>',
    apply_form = 'https://adelaideuni.edu.au/study/degrees/bachelor-of-oral-health/',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE cricos_course_code = '036335B';

-- Course: Bachelor of International Relations (022493C)
UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<p>Step into the exciting world of international relations, where you’ll uncover insights into today’s critical global challenges and explore Australia’s essential role in the Indo-Pacific and its commitment to regional security. Discover how health crises shape global politics and how social media transforms diplomacy. </p><p>Take on real-world challenges, bridging diverse cultures and political systems. Experience a hands-on blend of theory with case studies and immersive simulations. Build your industry connections by collaborating with top researchers and experts. </p><p>Sharpen your critical thinking, research, and communication skills, and develop a deep cross-cultural awareness. With these tools, you’ll be ready to analyse complex geopolitical issues and craft informed policy responses. </p><p>If a career in diplomacy calls to you, you could make a meaningful impact in diplomatic service, international organisations or non-governmental organisations. </p>',
